<worksheet>
<title>Phase portraits for linear systems with real distinct eigenvalues</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
            <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with a positive and negative eigenvalues.</li>
            
                <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with two negative eigenvalues.</li>
                    <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with two positive  eigenvalues.</li>
        </ul>    
</objectives>
<introduction>
    <p>
        In this worksheet we will discuss the cases of the phase portraits for the linear
                system
                <md>
                    \frac{d\vec{Y}}{dt}=A\vec{Y}
                </md>
                where <m>A</m> is a <m>2\times 2</m> matrix over <m>\mathbb{R}</m>, based on the
                values of the eigenvalues of <m>A</m>.
    </p>
</introduction>
    <section>
        <title><p>
                    Saddles ( <m>\lambda_{1}&lt;0&lt;\lambda_{2}</m> )
                </p></title>
        
        <example>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;x+2y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;3x+2y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task workspace="0.1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="1.0in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find and plot the straight line solutions.
                </p>
            </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                                                <md>
                                                    \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}e^{\lambda_1 t}\vec{V_1}+c_{2}e^{\lambda_2 t}\vec{V_2}.
                                                </md>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(4,3)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </example>
    </section>



<section>
        <title><p>
                     Sinks ( <m>\lambda_{1}&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;0</m> ) 
                </p></title>
        
        <exercise>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;-2x+y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;x-2y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task workspace="0.1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find and plot the straight line solutions.
                </p>
            </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                                                <md>
                                                    \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}e^{\lambda_1 t}\vec{V_1}+c_{2}e^{\lambda_2 t}\vec{V_2}.
                                                </md>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(2,4)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace=".5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </exercise>
    </section>



<section>
        <title><p>
                     Sources ( <m>0&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;\lambda_{1}</m> ) 
                </p></title>
        
        <exercise>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;x-y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;2x+4y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                                        
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task workspace="0.5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="0.2in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find and plot the straight line solutions.
                </p>
            </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                                                <md>
                                                    \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}e^{\lambda_1 t}\vec{V_1}+c_{2}e^{\lambda_2 t}\vec{V_2}.
                                                </md>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(1,1)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace=".5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </exercise>
    </section>


</worksheet>